  ('DOC012-C1', 'DOC012', 1, 'Hand Hygiene Policy', 'Infection Prevention', 'policy', '2026-01-01', 'Hand Hygiene Policy. Clean hands at the five moments: before touching a patient, before a clean or aseptic task, after body fluid exposure, after touching a patient, and after touching patient surroundings.'),
  ('DOC012-C2', 'DOC012', 2, 'Hand Hygiene Policy', 'Infection Prevention', 'policy', '2026-01-01', 'Hand Hygiene Policy. Artificial nails and nail extensions are not allowed for staff who give direct patient care.'),
  ('DOC012-C3', 'DOC012', 3, 'Hand Hygiene Policy', 'Infection Prevention', 'policy', '2026-01-01', 'Hand Hygiene Policy. Each unit is audited monthly. The compliance target is 95 percent, and results are posted on the unit quality board.'),
